  "final_visual_description": "A full-screen 16:9 restaurant TV menu with a warm cream background. The left side contains a compact but highly readable menu hierarchy: a small uppercase category label at the top, followed by a very large bold 'BOWLS' heading. Beneath it are three clearly separated menu items, each using a large uppercase dish name aligned left, a clearly visible price aligned right, and a short two-line description underneath. The right side is dominated by a large circular professional food photograph showing a colorful bowl with grilled chicken, vegetables, rice, beans, corn, avocado and greens. The food image occupies most of the right half and acts as the primary visual attraction. The composition has generous empty space around the typography, strong contrast, large fonts, and no interactive elements. It is specifically optimized for customers standing several meters away from a wall-mounted restaurant TV rather than for viewing on a phone or website."
  },
