  "overall_visual_description": "A full-screen 16:9 restaurant TV menu displaying the entire menu at once. A softly blurred, warm restaurant or food photograph fills the background, creating atmosphere without competing with the menu. Three clearly separated columns sit across the screen: Drinks on the left, Food in the center, and Packages on the right. Each category has an elegant white heading positioned above a collection of light cream rounded cards. Larger featured cards contain attractive food or drink photographs with the item name, short description, and price, while smaller products are arranged beneath them in compact rows with small thumbnails, descriptions, and prices. The cards create a clean information layer over the photographic background. The result feels like a premium restaurant digital signage screen rather than a website: no navigation bars, no buttons, no scrolling, and no unnecessary interface elements. The entire menu remains visible simultaneously so a customer can understand the available categories and scan prices from several meters away."
